 "how": "the seat's sealed tests and labelled explorations of 2026-10-22 and 2026-10-23 in main's fibre frame, read in full: the zero-free census (exploratory, labelled), ZERO_FREE_HOLOMORPHIC, TICK_LINE_HIGGS, TWO_HIGGS, the rule for threads with ingredients, and the framing check that reads across them. Each rule was committed before its script, each output before it was read, failures included, and each note says what its calibration does not count (menus, lines and readings chosen after earlier results; a lepton factor put in by hand). THE OUTCOMES AS THE SEAT'S OWN SEALED READINGS STATE THEM, in words: ZERO_FREE_HOLOMORPHIC's positive branch does not apply (the menu fits the coarse pattern on new points but not specifically, and holomorphy does not pick the reading); TICK_LINE_HIGGS's five pattern cells hold on lines chosen after the census, its CP cell fails, and one relation fails by construction; TWO_HIGGS's precision cell for the six mass ratios holds with a pair of directions chosen by the data out of six, its cell for the nine fails, so by the seat's own standing commitment the ingredient does not reach the values, and the tension between masses and mixing survives; the threads test is negative as the seat reports. MAIN READ THIS IN FULL AND COMPARES NOTHING: it sets outputs of a frame beside measured values under a rule of the seat's own; main recomputes nothing against data and repeats no measured value in its record. The frame instrument is main's (B1720). Main read the three files that bear on its own sealed arc B1740 only after that arc's outputs were committed, as it had pledged (B1740's page says so; harvest rows 1338, 1340 and 1342 had gone on saying 'unread' and are corrected today). The two sealed Higgs tests wait at register row P-316 for the comparison step, which main takes only under a sealed rule and the author's word",
